2. First fix: main layout spacing
Open:

frontend/src/assets/styles/components.css

Find this code:
.app-main {
  flex: 1;
  min-width: 0;
  margin-left: 260px;
}


Replace it with:
.app-main {
  flex: 1;
  min-width: 0;
  width: calc(100% - 252px);
  margin-left: 0;
  display: flex;
  flex-direction: column;
}

.page-content {
  width: 100%;
  max-width: 1600px;
  margin: 0 auto;
  padding: 24px 28px;
}


Then find the mobile responsive section:
@media (max-width: 768px) {
  .app-main {
    margin-left: 0;
  }
}


Replace it with:
@media (max-width: 768px) {
  .app-main {
    width: 100%;
  }

  .page-content {
    padding: 18px 14px;
  }
}


This removes the extra left spacing. We will connect the mobile sidebar in the next step.
3. Second fix: connect the mobile menu
Your App.jsx already has menuOpen state, but it is not passed to the Sidebar.

In App.jsx, find:
<Sidebar
  activePath={activePath}
  onNavigate={handleNavigate}
/>


Replace it with:
<Sidebar
  activePath={activePath}
  onNavigate={handleNavigate}
  isOpen={menuOpen}
/>


Now open Sidebar.jsx.

Change the function declaration:
export default function Sidebar({ activePath = '/dashboard', onNavigate }) {


To:
export default function Sidebar({
  activePath = '/dashboard',
  onNavigate,
  isOpen = false
}) {


Then change the <aside>:
<aside className={`sidebar ${isOpen ? 'sidebar-open' : ''}`}>


Add this CSS at the bottom of components.css:
@media (max-width: 768px) {
  .sidebar {
    position: fixed;
    top: 0;
    left: 0;
    bottom: 0;
    z-index: 1000;
    width: 252px;
    min-height: 100vh;
    transform: translateX(-100%);
    transition: transform 0.25s ease;
  }

  .sidebar.sidebar-open {
    transform: translateX(0);
  }

  .app-header {
    position: sticky;
    top: 0;
    z-index: 10;
  }
}


Your existing Header already calls onMenuClick, so the menu button will now control the sidebar.
